{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":3576010,"ns":0,"title":"Adaptive bias","extract":"Adaptive bias is the idea that the human brain has evolved to reason adaptively, rather than truthfully or even rationally, and that cognitive bias may have evolved as a mechanism to reduce the overall cost of cognitive errors as opposed to merely reducing the number of cognitive errors, when faced with making a decision under conditions of uncertainty.","description":"Theory of bias in human reasoning","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}